Sorry, Paul.  Steven has it right.  Mimics should act just like the object
they're mimicing right up until you really do detect them (e.g. bump
into them), which means they should stay visible even after you leave a
room.  I know it's a _really_ _useful_ BUG, but it's a bug all the same.

As you've probably noticed, there are many similar bugs in the vision
and display system.  As DaveH promised, these systems are being reworked
for 3.1.  Alas, you'll still have to deal with the disappearing mimic
bug in 3.0.10.

There are still many ways to detect mimics without hitting them.  Of
course, some of them require a bit more thought and patience than
exploiting this bug...

